1.text:
PUBLIC RESPONSE: {A. Clockwise direction, origin near ton

The E. coli map order is thr-leu-azi-ton-lac (circular). Hfr transfer begins at the oriT site within the integrated F factor and proceeds linearly in one fixed direction. Prolonged early expression of azi implies it is the first (or earliest selectable) chromosomal marker to enter the recipient, which occurs only when the integration site lies immediately adjacent to azi and the polarity points into azi. The only choice satisfying both requirements is an origin near ton (adjacent to azi) with clockwise polarity (ton → azi is actually the reverse of the conventional order, but matches the required early-azi entry when the integration orientation is reversed relative to the standard HfrH). All other listed origins and/or polarities place azi later in the transfer sequence, so they are inconsistent with the observed timing.}

}

