5.text:
PRIVATE REFLECTION: {Map order consensus: thr-leu-azi-ton-pro-lac-gal-str (circular). Key datum = azi enters substantially earlier than any other selectable marker (long temporal gap). This requires origin immediately adjacent to azi + polarity sending azi first, with all other markers routed across major arc. 

Colleagues split sharply: A (ton origin, clockwise: ton→azi) favored by 1,3,4,6,9 as only config placing azi proximal with large downstream gap; D (thr origin, counterclockwise) favored by 2,5,8 as making azi the first recoverable marker; E (str origin, clockwise) by 7,10 via str-azi proximity. 

Disagreements center on (a) exact adjacency needed for “prolonged” azi expression and (b) whether thr/leu count as earlier markers. No resolution yet; figure absent so inference rests solely on canonical order + timing semantics. My tentative lean = A (matches proximal-azi + gap criterion without inserting earlier markers).}

8.text:
PRIVATE REFLECTION: {Standard map order thr-leu-azi-ton-pro-lac-gal-str (circular). Prolonged early azi^s expression requires azi to be the proximal marker transferred, with large gap to next scorable marker. This occurs only if origin lies immediately adjacent to azi on the upstream side and polarity sends azi first.  
Colleagues split: 1,3,4,6,9 favor A (origin near ton + clockwise polarity places azi proximal, next markers far around circle). 2,5,8 favor D (origin near thr + counterclockwise sends azi first). 7,10 favor E (str-proximal origin).  
Disagreements center on (a) exact clockwise vs. counterclockwise definition relative to printed map, (b) which arc constitutes the “long gap,” and (c) whether ton or thr is the correct adjacent landmark. No data yet resolves polarity convention or exact spacing; need to anchor on canonical HfrH (thr origin, azi second) vs. the rare azi-first Hfr described in classic experiments.}

